## Lab Templates & Scripts

The `templates/` directory provides reusable building blocks for this lab:

### Terraform Module — `templates/terraform/modules/raspi-k8s/`

An umbrella Terraform module that composes all common Kubernetes resources in one call.
Supported child modules (all optional via feature flags):

| Module | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `deployment` | `Deployment` with configurable image, replicas, resources, probes |
| `service` | `Service` (ClusterIP / NodePort / LoadBalancer) |
| `ingress` | nginx `Ingress` with optional TLS via cert-manager |
| `namespace` | `Namespace` creation |
| `configmap` | Arbitrary `ConfigMap` |
| `secret` | Opaque `Secret` (base64-encoded data map) |
| `longhorn-pvc` | `PersistentVolumeClaim` on `longhorn` |
| `synology-pvc` | `PersistentVolumeClaim` on `synology-iscsi` |
| `local-pvc` | `PersistentVolumeClaim` on `local-storage` |
| `rbac` | `ServiceAccount` + `ClusterRoleBinding` |
| `monitoring` | Grafana `ConfigMap` dashboard injection |
| `registry` | `Secret` for private registry pull credentials |
| `tls-cert` | `Certificate` resource for cert-manager |

Usage pattern:
```hcl
module "myapp" {
  source         = "../../modules/raspi-k8s"
  name           = "myapp"
  namespace      = "default"
  image          = "{{REGISTRY_ADDRESS}}/myapp:latest"
  enable_ingress = true
  ingress_host   = "myapp.local"
}
```

Ready-made examples in `templates/terraform/examples/`:
- `simple-web-app/` — ClusterIP service + nginx Ingress, 2 replicas
- `postgres-synology/` — StatefulDB with `synology-iscsi` PVC and Kubernetes Secret

### Build & Push Script — `templates/scripts/build-push.sh`

Builds a multi-platform Docker image (`linux/arm64`) and pushes it to the lab registry.

```bash
# Basic: image name defaults to directory name
./templates/scripts/build-push.sh ./apps/api

# Custom name and tag
./templates/scripts/build-push.sh ./apps/api myapi:v2.1.0

# Override registry (also read automatically from inventory.ini)
REGISTRY={{REGISTRY_ADDRESS}} ./templates/scripts/build-push.sh ./apps/api
```

The script reads `inventory.ini` automatically to resolve the registry address.

